WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.920
Horror movies are always at their best when
the third act goes a little off the rails.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.870
Thriller endings are supposed to leave us
feeling either satisfied or completely unsatisfied,

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.130
and nowhere in between.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:15.730
So, when a scary movie actually delivers that
grand finale that ties all its terror tricks

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:17.890
together, it can be pretty unforgettable.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:21.449
Let's take a look back at some of those horror
flicks that really stuck the landing before

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:22.670
the turn of the millennium.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:26.939
And, it should go without saying, spoilers
for these old movies lay ahead...

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:30.300
The Omen
Directed by Richard Donner, The Omen features

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.500
one of the most iconic villains of all time:
Damien Thorn, a pint-sized Antichrist destined

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.010
to rule the world.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.230
Adopted by an American ambassador, Damien
is indoctrinated by his satanic nanny.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:43.430
Soon, the body count starts stacking up.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:47.980
After realizing his adopted kid is actually
the son of Satan, Daddy Thorn takes Damien

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.920
to a church and plans to go full-bore biblical
on him.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.210
We're talking Abraham and Isaac.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.180
"No, Daddy, no!"

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.160
"God help me."

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.800
However, before he can finish the dastardly
deed, the cops show up and open fire.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.790
After the gunsmoke clears, we cut to a funeral.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:09.250
But unfortunately for mankind, Damien is alive
and well — it's Thorn who's six feet under.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:13.500
And in a satanic twist of fate, Damien has
been adopted by Thorn's old buddy — the

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.750
President of the United States.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.060
Damien looks directly at the camera and gives
an eerie smile that'd easily prevent anyone

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.640
watching from ever wanting kids.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.610
Invasion of the Body Snatchers
In Philip Kaufman's Invasion of the Body Snatchers

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:31.710
remake, Donald Sutherland plays a San Francisco
health inspector named Matthew Bennell who's

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:35.450
drawn into a bizarre conspiracy involving
an evil alien race.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:39.510
These extraterrestrials are creating doppelgängers
of every human on Earth, and their plan is

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:44.580
to absorb victims while they sleep and create
emotionless doubles using plant-like pods.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.140
The process is horrifying.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.310
Naturally, this doesn't sit well with Bennell
and his small group of survivors, who desperately

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.210
try to stay awake to avoid having their bodies
snatched.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:57.360
The group also discovers they can fool the
aliens by acting cool and detached.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.930
But if they show an ounce of emotion, the
pod people emit a high-pitched scream to alert

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.370
their fellow aliens.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:03.120
It sounds like this:

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.860
(shrieking)

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:09.899
Bennell does his best to prevent the bad guys
from spreading their pods across the world,

00:02:09.899 --> 00:02:11.690
but there's no stopping the invasion.

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:15.720
At the end of the film, it appears that Bennell
is hiding from the bad guys in plain sight,

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.750
surviving by impersonating the pod people.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.849
But as he leaves his office one day, he runs
into an old friend who's still human...and

00:02:21.849 --> 00:02:23.760
that's when this happens:

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:29.760
(shrieking)

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:35.120
Friday the 13th
The horror genre is full of last-minute gotcha

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:38.680
moments, from the graveyard dream in Carrie
to the return of Freddy in A Nightmare on

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:39.680
Elm Street.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.829
But as good as those are, Friday the 13th's
finish stands decapitated head and shoulders

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:45.090
above the rest.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:49.400
This slasher classic follows a bunch of teenage
counselors fooling around at a summer camp

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:53.650
when a mysterious maniac turns up, slashing
folks with every sharp instrument known to

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:54.650
man.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:58.169
Eventually, the culprit is revealed to be
an angry Mrs. Voorhees, a former camp cook

00:02:58.169 --> 00:03:02.109
who wants revenge against all counselors for
letting her deformed son drown in Crystal

00:03:02.109 --> 00:03:03.629
Lake decades ago.

00:03:03.629 --> 00:03:08.010
Luckily, final girl Alice neck-chops Mrs.
Voorhees and escapes the camp by climbing

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.340
into a canoe and sailing onto the lake.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.099
She falls asleep before reaching the shore,
and when she wakes up, it's a beautiful day,

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:17.440
the cops have arrived, and it seems like she's
finally safe.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:21.489
And that's when a waterlogged Jason jumps
out of the lake and pulls Alice down with

00:03:21.489 --> 00:03:22.489
him.

00:03:22.489 --> 00:03:25.290
Alice later wakes up in a hospital, with no
sign of Jason anywhere.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.549
But she's not convinced he was some figment
of her fatigued imagination.

00:03:28.549 --> 00:03:31.829
"Then he's still there."

00:03:31.829 --> 00:03:35.830
No one believed her then — but the dozen
films to follow certainly proved she was right

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:37.069
about that.

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:40.129
The Thing
Directed by John Carpenter, The Thing is a

00:03:40.129 --> 00:03:44.340
brutally cynical sci-fi film that follows
a group of American scientists trapped inside

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.379
an Antarctic research station.

00:03:46.379 --> 00:03:50.689
They're being hunted by a shapeshifting alien
that absorbs its victims and creates identical

00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:55.680
copies, so in addition to battling this otherworldly
beast, our heroes are also dealing with a

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.439
serious case of paranoia.

00:03:57.439 --> 00:04:01.140
By the film's last act, the titular thing
has slain almost everyone in the camp, with

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:06.080
the exception of MacReady, a bearded helicopter
pilot who blows the creature to kingdom come.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:09.489
Unfortunately, he sets the entire base on
fire in the process.

00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:13.699
As he sits alone in the wreckage, that's when
Childs, MacReady's old frenemy steps in.

00:04:13.699 --> 00:04:17.639
The guy vanished during the climactic showdown
with the thing, and now MacReady isn't sure

00:04:17.639 --> 00:04:19.299
if Childs is human anymore.

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:22.860
The two are in a standoff, and as the cold
sets in, they share a bottle of whiskey and

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:27.560
wait for someone — or something — to make
the next move, leaving us to wonder if our

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:30.091
heroes will make it out alive…or if they're
even heroes anymore.

00:04:30.091 --> 00:04:37.650
"If we've got any surprises for each other,
I don't think we're in much shape to do anything

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:38.650
about it."

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:42.479
If you're gonna punctuate a pic with a question
mark, this is how it's done.

00:04:42.479 --> 00:04:45.699
Don't Look Now
After their daughter tragically drowns at

00:04:45.699 --> 00:04:50.610
their English estate, John and Laura Baxter
find themselves trapped in a spiral of grief.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:54.520
Devastated, they move to Venice, where they
encounter two creepy sisters who claim they

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.389
can see the little girl's spirit.

00:04:56.389 --> 00:04:59.139
Laura believes the psychic siblings, but John
is skeptical.

00:04:59.139 --> 00:05:02.300
Nevertheless, he does notice that something
weird is going on.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.669
There's a mysterious little figure running
around town, wearing the same red coat his

00:05:05.669 --> 00:05:07.370
daughter had on when she drowned.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:10.620
There are also rumors of a serial slayer in
the area.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:15.479
Stranger still, after his wife returns to
England on an emergency visit, John inexplicably

00:05:15.479 --> 00:05:18.979
spots her riding a funeral boat down a Venetian
canal.

00:05:18.979 --> 00:05:22.289
John's unease grows, until he spots the girl
in red one last time.

00:05:22.289 --> 00:05:26.669
Hoping that maybe it's the ghost of his daughter,
he follows the cloaked figure...only to realize

00:05:26.669 --> 00:05:30.439
it's actually a monstrous dwarf armed with
a meat cleaver!

00:05:30.439 --> 00:05:32.910
This is who's been dropping victims in the
Grand Canal.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:37.241
She plants her knife right into John's neck,
and as his body violently convulses, John

00:05:37.241 --> 00:05:41.599
realizes the vision of his wife on a funeral
boat was actually a premonition of his own

00:05:41.599 --> 00:05:42.599
demise.

00:05:42.599 --> 00:05:46.409
But there's nothing he can about it as he
bleeds out on the floor — a victim of grief,

00:05:46.409 --> 00:05:48.669
guilt, and one ugly monster.

00:05:48.669 --> 00:05:50.689
Talk about a tragic twist.

00:05:50.689 --> 00:05:53.510
In the Mouth of Madness
Equal parts H.P.

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:57.380
Lovecraft and Stephen King, In the Mouth of
Madness will make you feel like you're losing

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.380
your mind.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:02.660
In it, John Trent is an insurance investigator
hired by a publishing company to track down

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.610
bestselling author Sutter Cane.

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:08.110
The writer has mysteriously vanished, taking
his new novel with him.

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:11.990
But as Trent digs deeper into the case, he
learns that Cane is no average author.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:17.009
See, Cane has millions of loyal followers
around the world who worship his novels...which

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.320
gives him the power to bring his characters
to life.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:23.310
Worse still, Cane's new book will drive people
mad and turn them into monsters.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:26.719
It's all part of his scheme to destroy the
human race and subject humanity to the rule

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:27.990
of ancient gods.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:32.740
But before Cane can accomplish his plan, he
wants Trent to deliver his now-finished manuscript

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:37.470
to his publisher… and Trent has to obey
because he's actually one of Cane's characters.

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:40.479
Obviously, Trent refuses to believe he was
dreamed up for some book.

00:06:40.479 --> 00:06:44.360
But soon enough, Cane's novel has turned the
world into a mutated madhouse.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:48.290
With society crumbling around him and his
mind slowly slipping, Trent winds up in a

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:51.389
movie theater and watches the film adaptation
of Cane's book.

00:06:51.389 --> 00:06:54.630
As it turns out, Trent is the main character
and everything that's just happened to him

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.580
is playing on the big screen.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:07:00.819
Realizing his life is a Sutter Cane creation,
Trent snaps, laughing hysterically before

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:02.550
weeping uncontrollably.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:03.550
But hey!

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:05.729
At least he has the entire theater to himself.

00:07:05.729 --> 00:07:09.830
The Blair Witch Project
Nearly 20 years later, it's easy to forget

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:14.069
how big a deal The Blair Witch Project was
when it first debuted in 1999.

00:07:14.069 --> 00:07:18.479
It revolutionized viral marketing, introduced
the found footage fad to the mainstream, and

00:07:18.479 --> 00:07:21.729
totally messed people up with its incredibly
freaky ending.

00:07:21.729 --> 00:07:25.870
After heading into the woods to make a documentary
about the local legend of the Blair Witch,

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:30.139
three college students — Heather, Mike,
and Josh — find themselves completely lost

00:07:30.139 --> 00:07:31.509
and wandering in circles.

00:07:31.509 --> 00:07:32.620
"I gave you the map!"

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.479
"I gave you back the map!"

00:07:35.479 --> 00:07:40.129
They soon discover spooky stick figures hanging
from branches, hear creepy kids giggling at

00:07:40.129 --> 00:07:44.870
night, and then Josh mysteriously disappears,
leaving only a few teeth and a piece of his

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.039
tongue behind.

00:07:46.039 --> 00:07:49.939
Soon after, Mike and Heather hear him screaming
in the distance, and they follow the sound

00:07:49.939 --> 00:07:51.659
to an abandoned house.

00:07:51.659 --> 00:07:55.069
Camera in hand, Heather makes her way into
the basement and finds her friend standing

00:07:55.069 --> 00:07:59.659
in a corner…which is how a child slayer
of local legend would position his victims.

00:07:59.659 --> 00:08:03.750
That's when someone — or something — attacks
her from behind and the camera falls to the

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:07.689
ground, still recording for several seconds
before it stops.

00:08:07.689 --> 00:08:10.439
Psycho
It's a bit of a shock in Psycho when the main

00:08:10.439 --> 00:08:15.509
character, Marion Crane, is suddenly and violently
dispatched in the middle of the film.

00:08:15.509 --> 00:08:19.409
But things take an even crazier turn when
it's revealed that the culprit is hotel manager

00:08:19.409 --> 00:08:21.189
Norman Bates in drag.

00:08:21.189 --> 00:08:25.160
Having offed his own mother years ago, the
disturbed motel clerk suffers from a split

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:29.810
personality that causes him to act like his
evil mom and stab unsuspecting victims as

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:30.810
they shower.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.960
"We all go a little mad sometimes."

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:40.320
Norman is eventually captured and tossed into
a cell, where he completely transforms into

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.720
his domineering mother.

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:45.500
Huddled beneath a blanket with his mom's voice
running through his head, Norman looks at

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:50.130
the audience and gives a chilling grin, as
Mrs. Bates' skull flashes over his face, proving

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.760
that there is no more Norman — only Mom.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:56.220
We then cut back to the Bates Motel, where
the cops are towing Marion's car out of a

00:08:56.220 --> 00:09:00.870
swamp, leaving the viewer to wonder how many
more cars will be found down there.

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:04.880
Night of the Living Dead
This seminal zombie film has a simple plot:

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:08.660
one fateful day, corpses rise up from the
ground — and boy, are they hungry.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:13.130
Soon, a small band of survivors find themselves
trapped inside an old farmhouse, desperately

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:17.330
fighting the zombie horde, not to mention
their own growing fears and rivalries.

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:21.410
Eventually, there's only one survivor left,
a black man named Ben, who wakes up the next

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:24.340
morning after hearing a volley of gunshots
in the distance.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:29.450
Cautious but hopeful, Ben peers out the window,
spotting an all-white posse outside.

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:34.230
Suddenly, the gun-toting group sees Ben, and
assuming he's a zombie, a gunman puts a bullet

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:35.230
in his head.

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:39.660
Having survived an assault by an army of flesh-hungry
fiends, our hero is ultimately defeated by

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:42.650
the very people who were supposed to keep
him safe.

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:43.890
"Okay, he's dead.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:44.890
Let's go get him.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.320
That's another one for the fire."

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:49.640
There are a lot of social and political undertones
that can be drawn from the ending.

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:53.480
But the film lets the scene speak for itself
— a stroke of brilliance on director George

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:55.080
A. Romero's part.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:58.440
The Sixth Sense
In the movie that put M. Night Shyamalan on

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:02.770
the map, we meet child psychologist Malcolm
Crowe, who has some unfinished business to

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:03.970
attend to.

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:07.930
Years after failing to help a young patient
suffering from hallucinations, he gets a shot

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:10.790
at redemption in the form of nine-year-old
Cole Sear.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:16.260
And folks, Cole has a heck of a problem:
"I see dead people."

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:19.310
Cole reveals that the people he sees don't
know they aren't alive.

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:23.630
And while the doctor is skeptical at first,
he quickly learns the boy really does possess,

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:26.110
well, a sixth sense.

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:29.740
Realizing the spirits might need help, Crowe
encourages Cole to communicate with the ghosts

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:31.490
and come to terms with his gift.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:35.060
Meanwhile, Crowe has grown distant from his
wife, and at the end of the movie, he sits

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:38.990
beside his sleeping bride — which is when
the director's famous knack for twists kicks

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:39.990
in.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:44.250
In her sleep, Crowe's wife asks why he left
her and then drops something on the floor.

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:48.450
It's Crowe's wedding ring…the one he thought
he was wearing during the whole film.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:52.220
Suddenly Crowe remembers that a disgruntled
patient — the one he'd failed so long ago

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:55.670
— actually ended his life before doing the
same to himself.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:58.860
Crowe's been a ghost all along, and the clues
were everywhere.

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:00.540
It doesn't get much better than that.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:01.600
Thanks for watching!

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:04.060
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:06.110
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

